eval("__webpack_require__.r(__webpack_exports__);\n/* harmony export */ __webpack_require__.d(__webpack_exports__, {\n/* harmony export */   devotionalProduct: () => (/* binding */ devotionalProduct),\n/* harmony export */   initialDevotionals: () => (/* binding */ initialDevotionals)\n/* harmony export */ });\nconst devotionalProduct = {\n    title: \"Engaging Babylon\",\n    subtitle: \"30 Days of Daily Devotionals and Prayer: Standing Firm in Faith, Navigating Influence, and Advancing God's Kingdom in a Changing World\",\n    coverImage: \"/images/Cover%20newest.jpg\",\n    description: \"This 30-day devotional is developed from Engaging Babylon: Navigating Faith and Influence in an Increasingly Godless World by Tolulope Toluwase. It follows the book's central message: you can enter systems of influence, pursue excellence, receive opportunities, and rise to prominence without surrendering your identity, convictions, or allegiance to God.\\n\\nThe devotional draws particularly from the book's teaching on Daniel and his companions, the subtle process of spiritual compromise, discernment, consecration, wisdom, godly community, prayer, eternal perspective, and the responsibility that comes with influence.\\n\\nThe goal is not merely to help you recognise the pressures of the world, but to equip you to live faithfully within it—to become a person through whom God's wisdom, character, and purposes are revealed.\",\n    purchaseLinks: [\n        {\n            label: \"Buy on Selar\",\n            url: \"https://selar.com/14c5ew1174\"\n        },\n        {\n            label: \"Buy on Amazon Kindle\",\n            url: \"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0HP28M6RH/ref=sr_1_2?dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.rD8j7pct73PKk9UENFS6Adk_MZYzdZAWhUXSMZlxUrU.5MgsYhsPd5meynZ9FUVEjv5Pj94txHD7r_ZYYvA2WXE&dib_tag=se&qid=1792842409&refinements=p_27%3ATOLULOPE+TOLUWASE&s=digital-text&sr=1-2&text=TOLULOPE+TOLUWASE\"\n        }\n    ]\n};\nconst initialDevotionals = [\n    {\n        id: \"dev-1\",\n        slug: \"the-fire-on-the-altar-must-not-go-out\",\n        title: \"The Fire on the Altar Must Not Go Out\",\n        date: \"2026-10-22\",\n        scriptureReference: \"Leviticus 6:12-13\",\n        scriptureText: \"The fire on the altar must be kept burning; it must not go out. Every morning the priest is to add firewood and arrange the burnt offering on the fire and burn the fat of the fellowship offerings on it. The fire must be kept burning on the altar continuously; it must not go out.\",\n        excerpt: \"Revival is not an event we schedule; it is an atmosphere sustained by consecrated priests who refuse to let the fire die upon their secret altars.\",\n        content: [\n            \"There is a divine command whispered into the heart of every believer called to carry God’s presence in this hour: The fire must not go out. In the Old Testament economy, the origin of the altar fire was supernatural—God Himself sent fire from heaven. But the maintenance of that fire was entrusted to mortal hands. Every single morning, the priest had to gather wood, arrange the sacrifice, and clear away the ashes.\",\n            \"So many believers mourn the absence of spiritual passion, wondering why their prayers feel cold and their spirits sluggish. Yet heaven asks a simple question: Where is the morning wood? Where is the quiet consecration before the demands of the world scream for your attention? You cannot expect an evening revival on the momentum of yesterday’s ashes.\",\n            \"Clearing the ashes is just as essential as laying the wood. The ash represents past victories, old moves of God, and yesteryear’s encounters that have now cooled down. If you cling to the memory of how God moved five years ago without offering your heart today, the ashes will choke the living flame.\",\n            \"Beloved, God is calling you to a daily priesthood. Before you step out into your workplace, before you open your social media feeds, step before the sacred altar of His presence. Lay your pride, your anxieties, your calendar, and your voice upon the wood. When heaven sees the sacrifice in place, the holy flame will never diminish.\"\n        ],\n        reflectionQuestions: [\n            'What \"ashes\" of past achievements or old spiritual experiences are you holding onto that need to be cleared away for fresh fire?',\n            \"What practical commitment can you make this morning to bring fresh consecrated wood to your secret place?\"\n        ],\n        prayer: \"Lord God of Elijah, the God who answers by fire: I present my body and my life to You today as a living sacrifice. Cleanse my heart from lukewarmness and distractions. Set my secret place ablaze with the Holy Ghost. Let every compromise be consumed, and let my life burn as a continuous flame of worship to Your holy name. In Jesus’ mighty name, Amen.\",\n        tags: [\n            \"Revival\",\n            \"Prayer Altar\",\n            \"Consecration\",\n            \"Spiritual Discipline\"\n        ],\n        author: \"Evangelist Tolucci\",\n        readingTimeMinutes: 4\n    },\n    {\n        id: \"dev-2\",\n        slug: \"the-mystery-of-prophetic-sounds\",\n        title: \"The Mystery of Prophetic Sounds & Kingdom Songs\",\n        date: \"2026-10-21\",\n        scriptureReference: \"2 Kings 3:15\",\n        scriptureText: 'But now bring me a harpist. While the harpist was playing, the hand of the LORD came on Elisha and he said, \"This is what the LORD says: I will fill this valley with pools of water.\"',\n        excerpt: \"True Kingdom sound is not entertainment; it is spiritual frequency that dismantles demonic resistance and ushers in the tangible hand of the Lord.\",\n        content: [\n            \"Music in the Kingdom of God is far more than musical cadence or vocal gymnastics. When Prophet Elisha was confronted with three kings in desperate need of divine direction, he did not call for an intellectual symposium. He called for a minstrel. Scripture records that as the harpist touched the cords, the hand of the Lord came upon the prophet.\",\n            \"A true Kingdom sound carries spiritual weight. It is an auditory gateway that aligns the earthly realm with heavenly frequency. When David played his harp before King Saul, distressing spirits fled not because David was technically skilled—though he was—but because David’s sound was birthed from secret-place intimacy with Jehovah.\",\n            \"Today, the global church is saturated with noise, but crying out for sound. Noise stimulates the flesh, stirs superficial emotions, and leaves the soul barren after the beat fades. Sound, however, penetrates the marrow of the spirit. It births repentance, brings healing to broken bones, breaks chains of addiction, and commands water into dry valleys.\",\n            \"When you lift your voice in worship today, understand that you are releasing spiritual warfare. You are not singing to impress people or fill empty space. You are declaring the supremacy of the Lamb over your family, your city, and your destiny.\"\n        ],\n        reflectionQuestions: [\n            \"What kind of sounds and media are you allowing into your spiritual environment each day?\",\n            \"How can you shift your personal worship from mere musical appreciation into an altar of deep spiritual encounter?\"\n        ],\n        prayer: \"Father, attune my ears and my voice to the frequency of heaven. Deliver me from the superficial noise of this generation. Release upon my heart and home the prophetic sound of revival. As I worship You today, let Your hand fall mightily upon my life, breaking every chain and filling every dry valley with living water. In Jesus’ name, Amen.\",\n        tags: [\n            \"Prophetic Worship\",\n            \"Spiritual Warfare\",\n            \"Holy Spirit\",\n            \"Intimacy\"\n        ],\n        author: \"Evangelist Tolucci\",\n        readingTimeMinutes: 5\n    },\n    {\n        id: \"dev-3\",\n        slug: \"walking-in-the-power-of-the-spirit\",\n        title: \"Walking in the Power of the Holy Spirit\",\n        date: \"2026-10-20\",\n        scriptureReference: \"Zechariah 4:6\",\n        scriptureText: \"Not by might nor by power, but by my Spirit,’ says the LORD Almighty.\",\n        excerpt: \"Human intellect and physical strength will always exhaust themselves at the threshold of spiritual assignments. Only the Holy Ghost sustains Kingdom momentum.\",\n        content: [\n            \"We live in a culture obsessed with human hustle, branding, and charisma. Yet in the economy of the Kingdom of God, Zerubbabel stood before an immovable mountain and was reminded of an eternal law: the work of God cannot be finished by the arm of flesh.\",\n            \"To attempt spiritual ministry, righteous living, or Kingdom purpose without the continuous empowerment of the Holy Spirit is like pushing an automobile uphill with the engine turned off. You will sweat, you will grow disillusioned, and you will eventually burn out.\",\n            \"The Holy Spirit is not an impersonal force or an occasional visitor at Sunday service. He is the Third Person of the Godhead, sent to dwell inside you, to counsel you, to quicken your mortal body, and to release supernatural dunamis power through your life.\",\n            'When you yield your will to Him, the mountains that intimidated you become level ground. Doors that no man can shut open by divine grace. Begin today by saying, \"Holy Spirit, I cannot navigate this day without You. Take full possession of my mind, my tongue, and my steps.\"'\n        ],\n        reflectionQuestions: [\n            \"Where in your life have you been relying on your own strength and intellectual calculations rather than the Spirit?\",\n            \"How often do you consult the Holy Spirit during regular decisions throughout your day?\"\n        ],\n        prayer: \"Precious Holy Spirit, Breath of God, I surrender all to You. Forgive me for the times I have relied on my own wisdom and strength. Fill me afresh today. Quicken my spirit, guide my decisions, and let Your power flow unhindered through my hands and voice to bring glory to Jesus Christ. Amen.\",\n        tags: [\n            \"Holy Spirit\",\n            \"Power\",\n            \"Grace\",\n            \"Faith\"\n        ],\n        author: \"Evangelist Tolucci\",\n        readingTimeMinutes: 4\n    },\n    {\n        id: \"dev-4\",\n        slug: \"rebuilding-the-broken-gates\",\n        title: \"Rebuilding the Broken Gates of Prayer\",\n        date: \"2026-10-19\",\n        scriptureReference: \"Nehemiah 2:17\",\n        scriptureText: 'Then I said to them, \"You see the trouble we are in: Jerusalem lies in ruins, and its gates have been burned with fire. Come, let us rebuild the wall of Jerusalem, and we will no longer be in disgrace.\"',\n        excerpt: \"When the spiritual gates of a life or generation are broken, the enemy walks in unchallenged. God is raising watchmen who will rebuild the ancient gates.\",\n        content: [\n            \"In biblical antiquity, the gates of a city were where elders sat, where judicial verdicts were delivered, and where defense was coordinated. If the walls were strong but the gates were burned, the entire city was defenseless.\",\n            \"In our contemporary era, the enemy does not always need to tear down the physical walls of our churches or families; he simply targets the gates of prayer, discernment, and moral truth. When Christians stop praying, when families stop having family altars, the gates are effectively down.\",\n            \"Nehemiah wept, fasted, and prayed when he heard the report. But he did not stop at weeping. He arose, gathered the people with a trowel in one hand and a sword in the other, and rebuilt the gates despite mockers and fierce opposition.\",\n            \"Today, heaven is asking: Who will stand in the breach? Who will watch over their children at 3:00 AM? Who will intercede for the revival of our youth and our campuses? The gates must be repaired, and they are rebuilt on our knees.\"\n        ],\n        reflectionQuestions: [\n            \"What areas in your family, workplace, or personal walk have suffered due to broken prayer gates?\",\n            \"How can you establish a watchman’s posture for your generation?\"\n        ],\n        prayer: \"Lord of the Harvest, make me a watchman on the walls of Zion. I take my place at the gates today. Repair every broken hedge in my life, my home, and my ministry. Grant me grace to tarry in prayer until righteousness goes forth as brightness. In Jesus’ name, Amen.\",\n        tags: [\n            \"Prayer\",\n            \"Intercession\",\n            \"Spiritual Warfare\",\n            \"Watchmen\"\n        ],\n        author: \"Evangelist Tolucci\",\n        readingTimeMinutes: 4\n    }\n];\n//# sourceURL=[module]\n//# sourceMappingURL=data:application/json;charset=utf-8;base64,\n//# sourceURL=webpack-internal:///(ssr)/./src/data/devotionals.ts\n");

